    body: "President Zelensky has thanked the European Union for the support it has given to Ukraine, describing heads of state and government gathered in Brussels as \"real leaders\".\n\nMeanwhile, President Trump has said Ukraine's resumption of strikes on Russian oil refineries was a disgrace.\n\nZelensky made the comment flanked by European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen and European Council President António Costa.\n\nThe BBC's Nick Beake reports from Brussels.\n\nRelated topics\n\n- UkraineUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- Volodymyr ZelenskyUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- Donald TrumpUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- United StatesUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- War in UkraineUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.",
